After dinner, I sit down on the couch.
I take my phone and call home to my family in Mexico.
My sister, Sofía, answers with a big smile.
"Hi Maya!" she says happily.
"Hi Sofía, it is lovely to see you," I reply.
In the background, I see my brother, Diego.
He waves at me, and I wave back.
Then our dog, Lola, barks at the screen.
I smile, because she can probably recognize my voice.
We talk together about my day.
I tell them about my new job as a software engineer.
In Copenhagen it is dark, but I am doing well.
I am already looking forward to talking with them again.
